{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792745271,"nonce":"DxOWVF/Ln5EnB+TBjW7k668St8Q=","title":"Preserve project defines in every editor parse","message":"RayDE's external ashui/app/WindowedApp.hx is guarded by hlwindow || ashui_window. Current RayDE build configuration resolves hlwindow=0.3.1 correctly, and the workspace declaration parser can see WindowedApp. Full semantic analysis of WindowedApp exceeds the 120-second probe timeout in third-party macro dependencies; that remains a separate verification limitation.\n\nThe audit found that on-demand method signatures inherit the last canonically parsed file's preprocessor configuration, allowing a stdlib parse to remove project defines. Boolean preprocessing also discards -D values, lacks comparisons, and fails to expose the underscore spelling of hyphenated defines. HXML target flags were confined to user files rather than reaching stdlib conditional declarations.\n\nThe proposed fix preserves values and normalized spellings in parser and macro contexts, supports conditional comparisons, keeps user and stdlib signature views separate, and propagates target flags to stdlib parsing. Regression coverage includes external source paths, macro defines, included HXML changes and cached indexes.","files":null}]}